---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
// REVIEW DRAFT: Keep noIndex=true until the publication gates in PRIVACY_REVIEW.md are closed.
---

<SiteLayout
  page="privacy"
  title="Privacy Policy — Stimmyz"
  description="How Stimmyz handles audio, local soundboards, optional services, and privacy choices in the Android beta."
  themeColor="#fbfaf7"
  noIndex={true}
>
  <main id="main">
    <div class="container policy-top">
      <div class="eyebrow">YOUR PRIVACY MATTERS</div>
      <h1>Privacy Policy<span class="ink-accent">.</span></h1>
      <p>
        How Stimmyz handles recordings, imported sounds, artwork, and your choices.
      </p>
      <div class="policy-timestamp">
        Draft for approval · October 31, 2026 · Android beta and this website
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="container policy-content">
      <aside class="policy-toc">
        <strong>ON THIS PAGE</strong>
        <a href="#overview">Overview</a>
        <a href="#controller">Who is responsible for your information?</a>
        <a href="#access">Information used by the Android app</a>
        <a href="#analytics">Analytics in this beta</a>
        <a href="#storage">Where content is stored and how it can be shared</a>
        <a href="#retention">Backups, retention, and deletion</a>
        <a href="#website">Our website</a>
        <a href="#contacts">Email, feedback, and service providers</a>
        <a href="#purposes">Purposes and legal bases</a>
        <a href="#rights">Your choices and privacy rights</a>
        <a href="#children">Age audience</a>
        <a href="#changes">Changes to this policy</a>
      </aside>
      <article class="policy-article">
        <div class="draft-banner" role="note">
          <strong>Review draft — not yet approved for Google Play.</strong>
          Verify the owner and provider facts and complete the release checks in
          <code>website/PRIVACY_REVIEW.md</code> before publication.
        </div>
        <div class="policy-summary">
          <p>
            <strong>In short:</strong> The current Stimmyz Android beta keeps
            recordings, imported sounds, artwork, and boards locally. Usage analytics
            are disabled. Manual ZIP backups are user-controlled; website visits and
            contact messages are processed by service providers as explained below.
          </p>
        </div>
        <p>
          <strong>Last updated:</strong> October 31, 2026 (draft for owner approval;
          update to actual publication date).
        </p>
        <section aria-labelledby="overview">
          <h2 id="overview">1. Overview</h2>
          <p>
            Stimmyz is an Android soundboard app for recording, importing, trimming,
            saving, and playing short sound clips, adding artwork, and organizing clips
            into soundboards. The app is designed to keep sounds and board data on your
            device rather than in a Stimmyz cloud account.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>For the analytics-disabled beta described here, Stimmyz does not
            send usage-analytics events.</strong> The app includes an inactive PostHog
            software component, but its analytics transport is disabled in this build.
            There are no advertising integrations, app accounts, or cloud
            synchronization of your sounds in this release. If this changes in a future
            version, we will update this policy and provide any required choices before
            enabling the new processing.
          </p>
          <p>
            This policy covers the app, our website, and messages you send to us.
            Android, Google Play, your browser, and any email app you choose have their
            own privacy practices.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section aria-labelledby="controller">
          <h2 id="controller">2. Who is responsible for your information?</h2>
          <p>
            <strong>App and website:</strong> Stimmyz <br />
            <strong>Developer / data controller:</strong> Šarūnas Zubė, operating as
            Stimmyz <br />
            <strong>Privacy contact:</strong> <a href="mailto:privacy@stimmyz.app">
            privacy@stimmyz.app</a> <br />
            <strong>Support contact:</strong> <a href="mailto:support@stimmyz.app">
            support@stimmyz.app</a>
          </p>
          <p>
            Please use the privacy contact for questions about your data or requests to
            exercise privacy rights.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section aria-labelledby="access">
          <h2 id="access">3. Information used by the Android app</h2>
          <p>
            <strong>Device-playback audio.</strong> When you choose to capture sound
            playing on your device, Stimmyz asks for the Android capture authorization
            required for that session and processes only audio that Android and the
            source application permit to be captured. Some applications block playback
            capture. Android may display a foreground-service notification and a Stop
            control while capture is active.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Microphone audio.</strong> When you start a microphone recording,
            Stimmyz asks for microphone permission as required by Android and processes
            the audio to create your clip. Microphone recording is user-initiated.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Selected files and artwork.</strong> If you import an audio/video
            file or choose artwork, Android's file, photo, or document picker gives
            Stimmyz access to the item you select. The app may make its own local copy
            for editing and playback.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Saved content and settings.</strong> Stimmyz stores the clips you
            create or import, their names and edits, artwork, library entries, board/pad
            assignments, and preferences such as volume and appearance on your device.
            It also keeps local first-run and privacy-setting state necessary for the
            app to work.
          </p>
          <p>
            These features work without an account or optional analytics. Denying a
            feature-specific permission may prevent that feature from working, but does
            not disable unrelated soundboard features.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section aria-labelledby="analytics">
          <h2 id="analytics">4. Analytics in this beta</h2>
          <p>
            The Android beta covered by this policy has <strong>usage analytics disabled</strong>.
            No sound-creation, playback, board-use, or error analytics events are sent
            by Stimmyz in this build. The onboarding privacy screen explains this and
            does not activate tracking. You do not need to agree to analytics to use
            Stimmyz.
          </p>
          <p>
            The app may include inactive PostHog library code for a potential future
            opt-in beta. Its presence does not mean the current app sends analytics
            events. If we introduce optional analytics later, we will first update this
            notice, confirm the relevant privacy safeguards, and obtain any required
            valid consent. We will not transmit recordings, audio content, artwork, or
            sound names as product analytics.
          </p>
          <p>
            Earlier limited development/test versions may have sent optional analytics
            events when a tester opted in. Those historical records are separate from
            this disabled beta release. If you used an earlier test build and wish to
            ask about data previously sent, contact <a href="mailto:privacy@stimmyz.app">
            privacy@stimmyz.app</a>. We will assess the request against the provider's
            actual retention and deletion capabilities.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section aria-labelledby="storage">
          <h2 id="storage">5. Where content is stored and how it can be shared</h2>
          <p>
            Saved clips, imported copies, artwork, boards, and preferences are kept in
            app storage on your Android device. The analytics-disabled build does not
            upload them to a Stimmyz-operated media server. We use Android app isolation
            and system permission controls, but no device or application can be
            guaranteed completely secure.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you use an Android sharing option or intentionally export content, <strong>
            you choose the destination</strong>. Other apps or services that receive
            your shared files process them under their own terms.
          </p>
          <p>
            Stimmyz supports <strong>manual ZIP export and restore</strong>. A ZIP
            export can include saved sounds, referenced artwork, boards, and
            preferences. The app's first-run completion state, analytics consent state,
            and analytics identifiers are not included. Protect exported ZIP files
            because anyone with access to them may be able to access their contents.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section aria-labelledby="retention">
          <h2 id="retention">6. Backups, retention, and deletion</h2>
          <p>
            Stimmyz configures Android automatic cloud backup and device-to-device
            transfer to exclude its app data and sets Android backup to disabled.
            Behavior of every device manufacturer's own backup or transfer tools has not
            been verified, so the app cannot guarantee how every separate system or
            user-operated backup behaves.
          </p>
          <p>
            Your app-owned clips, artwork, boards, and settings remain locally until you
            delete the relevant content, clear the app's data, or uninstall it, subject
            to device behavior. <strong>Removing a sound from a board does not
            necessarily delete the sound from your Library.</strong> Deleting a sound
            from the Library removes the app-owned version as implemented by the app. It
            does not delete the original file you imported, a separately shared copy, or
            a ZIP you exported. You must manage those external copies yourself.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you delete the app or clear its data, we generally cannot restore locally
            stored sounds or recover them from a Stimmyz cloud account, because no such
            account exists.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section aria-labelledby="website">
          <h2 id="website">7. Our website</h2>
          <p>
            The website at <a href="https://stimmyz.app/">https://stimmyz.app/</a> is
            hosted using <strong>Vercel</strong>. Opening it causes your browser to send
            ordinary network requests that may include your IP address, browser/device
            information, requested URL, and request timestamps. The hosting service may
            process technical request and security logs needed to deliver and protect
            the website. <strong>Cloudflare</strong> provides domain and routing
            infrastructure.
          </p>
          <p>
            The website itself is not intentionally configured with advertising
            trackers, product analytics, or script-set tracking cookies in the reviewed
            version. Your browser and service providers may have their own network-level
            functions. Technical request and security logs are retained according to the
            hosting arrangement and applicable operational or security requirements. You
            can contact us for details about relevant retention periods and processing
            arrangements.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section aria-labelledby="contacts">
          <h2 id="contacts">8. Email, feedback, and service providers</h2>
          <p>
            If you choose <strong>Send feedback</strong> or contact us by email, Stimmyz
            opens your email app or Android sharing option. It does not automatically
            attach sound clips, application logs, or device identifiers. You decide
            whether to send the message and what it contains.
          </p>
          <p>
            We process the contact details, message contents, and any attachments you
            voluntarily send to respond to your inquiry, handle a privacy request, and
            follow up where necessary. Incoming messages to our domain are forwarded
            using <strong>Cloudflare Email Routing</strong> and delivered to a <strong>
            Google-hosted Gmail mailbox</strong>. Our email providers may process
            message routing data, sender and recipient addresses, message content,
            timestamps, and security metadata to provide these services. If an external
            email-delivery provider is used for replies, it may also process the
            recipient address, message content, and delivery metadata. We will update
            this policy when such a provider is used.
          </p>
          <p>
            We use correspondence for responding and resolving requests and for
            applicable legal obligations, not for advertising. We keep it only for the
            period needed to handle the issue, reasonable follow-up, and any applicable
            legal obligations or claims. We review correspondence for continued
            necessity and delete it when it is no longer needed, subject to applicable
            legal obligations.
          </p>
          <p>
            Third-party providers such as Vercel, Cloudflare, Google, and (in any future
            analytics-enabled release) PostHog may process information under their
            applicable service arrangements. Some processing may occur outside the
            European Economic Area. When an international transfer of personal data
            requires safeguards under applicable law, we are responsible for using an
            appropriate lawful transfer arrangement. Contact us for information about
            the arrangements that apply to a particular service.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section aria-labelledby="purposes">
          <h2 id="purposes">9. Purposes and legal bases</h2>
          <p>
            Where the GDPR applies to personal information processed by us or our
            service providers, we process it only for the purposes described above.
            Website operation and security, and responding to ordinary support requests,
            generally rely on our legitimate interests in operating, protecting, and
            supporting Stimmyz (GDPR Article 6(1)(f)), balanced against your rights.
            Where a legal duty applies, we may process data to meet that duty (Article
            6(1)(c)). Any future optional analytics that rely on consent will not be
            enabled without the required consent and disclosures.
          </p>
          <p>
            Audio and other content stored and processed only on your device are not
            uploaded to us by the current app. Granting an Android permission is not, by
            itself, consent to unrelated off-device analytics.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section aria-labelledby="rights">
          <h2 id="rights">10. Your choices and privacy rights</h2>
          <p>
            You can stop recordings, decline or revoke Android permissions, delete
            Library items, and clear app data using Android's controls. You can also
            avoid sending feedback or visiting the website.
          </p>
          <p>
            If applicable under privacy law, you may ask us for access to, correction or
            deletion of, or restriction of processing of personal information we hold
            about you; object to certain processing; and request data portability where
            applicable. If processing is based on consent, you may withdraw it without
            affecting earlier lawful processing. Email <a href="mailto:privacy@stimmyz.app">
            privacy@stimmyz.app</a> with your request. We may need enough information to
            verify that the request relates to you, but do not send passwords or private
            sound recordings unless specifically necessary and agreed.
          </p>
          <p>
            We cannot inspect or retrieve sound clips that remain only on your device.
            If you are in the European Economic Area, you also have the right to
            complain to your relevant supervisory authority; in Lithuania, this is the <strong>
            State Data Protection Inspectorate (VDAI)</strong>.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section aria-labelledby="children">
          <h2 id="children">11. Age audience</h2>
          <p>
            Stimmyz's intended beta audience is people aged <strong>16 and older</strong>.
            The app does not require an account or collect a date of birth in this
            build. Its intended audience is not a claim that each user's age is
            verified. Optional product analytics remain disabled for all users in this
            release.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you believe a child has sent personal information to us through a support
            message, please contact <a href="mailto:privacy@stimmyz.app">
            privacy@stimmyz.app</a> so we can review the situation.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section aria-labelledby="changes">
          <h2 id="changes">12. Changes to this policy</h2>
          <p>
            We may update this policy when the app, its data processing, service
            providers, or legal requirements change. We will publish the revised policy
            here with an updated date and provide additional notice or choice when
            required.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Privacy:</strong> <a href="mailto:privacy@stimmyz.app">
            privacy@stimmyz.app</a> <br />
            <strong>Support:</strong> <a href="mailto:support@stimmyz.app">
            support@stimmyz.app</a>
          </p>
        </section>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
